# Design Tokens

## Colors

Never hardcode colors in components. Import from `@/lib/constants/colors` or use CSS variables / Tailwind theme tokens from `globals.css`.

Approved palette:
- Magenta primary: `#E20A96` (hover `#C40882`)
- Dark navy: `#292D3D` (light `#373C52`)
- Soft pink: `#FCEAF4`
- Background grey: `#F7F7FA`
- Pure white: `#FFFFFF`
- Secondary text: `#53596A`
- Border: `#E8E8ED`

Prefer `text-navy`, `text-magenta`, `bg-pit-grey`, `bg-soft-pink`, `border-pit`, `btn-primary`, `btn-outline`.

Avoid generic template chrome: Sparkles pill badges, card-lift spam, purple/indigo gradients, dark-gold luxury themes.

## Typography

Never hardcode font families, sizes, or weights. Use `TYPO` / feature constants from `@/lib/constants/typography`. Load fonts via `next/font` — do not inject Google Fonts stylesheets in `<head>`.

## Styling

- No inline `style={{}}` — use `className` with Tailwind utilities or shared CSS classes (`pit-grid-bg`, `hero-pattern`).
- Dynamic visual values → add tokens to `globals.css` `@theme` / `:root`, reference via `var(--…)`.
- Patterns: calm editorial whitespace, navy hierarchy, magenta accents, subtle motion with `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Prefer CSS variables + `@theme` over arbitrary Tailwind value classes.
